# Second-brain rules

- Start at `INDEX.md`, then read `System/operating-status.md`,
  `System/approval-queue.md`, and `12_Brain/09_Ops/AGENT_PROTOCOL.md`.
- Search first and follow links. Do not sweep the whole vault into context.
- Keep client truth in `01_Clients/`. Use `12_Brain/` for captures, entities,
  concepts, decisions, projects, research, reviews, and memory.
- Captures are immutable receipts. Compiled notes must carry `source_refs`.
- Record durable decisions, corrections, and reusable lessons; do not record
  secrets or routine chatter.
- Use the two-output rule: deliver the requested artifact and make the smallest
  useful local memory update when durable knowledge was created.
- Run `System/scripts/Test-SecondBrain.ps1` before reporting substantive vault
  work complete.
